WEBVTT

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:32.340
Oh, no! You got me!

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.780
This feels great!

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.650
What are you doing, Hartmann?!

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.950
I'm taking a break and cooling off.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.530
You should come in too, Trude.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.780
We're in the middle of training! And anyway,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.050
Their performance is certainly remarkable.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.660
Everyone's doing all right.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.490
That day when I held up my hand

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.620
And saw a far-away light

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.280
Gertrud Barkhorn

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.280
Minna-Dietlinde Wilcke

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.760
Piercing between my fingers

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.760
I swore to the sky

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.870
Charlotte E. Yeager

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.870
Francesca Lucchini

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.800
I'd cut through this storm

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.740
Faster than the speed of sound

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.580
Perrine H. Closterman

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.990
On magic wings

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:55.230
To protect your smile

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.170
Eila Ilmatar Juutilainen

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.990
Painfully, I start to cry

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.820
But you come to my side again

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.680
I absolutely will not give up

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.710
This blue, blue place

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.000
"Come on, let's fly!"

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:16.100
If I could fly I'd shield you with

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.890
My overflowing courage

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.130
And I would shake off

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.400
The approaching dark

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.640
Stronger than yesterday

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.830
I will head into

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:37.570
That familiar, sparkling sky

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:52.150
St. Trond's Thunder

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:59.460
Faced with the appearance of a
massive Neuroi hive over Venezia,

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.980
In July of 1945, the joint military
forces put all efforts

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:06.410
Into launching Operation Mars.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.940
The combined armada and the Witches attacked
from the sea and the air.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:20.160
Due to the active frontal assault by the
501st Joint Fighter Wing, "Strike Witches",

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.660
The massive Neuroi hive was annihilated.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:24.960
Venezia was liberated.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.240
Afterwards, the unit was disbanded,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.580
And the Witches were assigned
to other parts of the world.

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.180
Half a month later,

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.930
Wing Commander Minna and other
members of the Karlsland Air Force

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.700
Became stationed at St. Trond in the Kingdom of Belgica.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.700
Kingdom of Belgica, St. Trond Base

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.440
It's been awhile since we've had good training.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:51.710
Imperial Government of Karlsland Air Force

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:51.710
Wing Commander Minna-Dietlinde Wilcke

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:51.710
Nevertheless, our night patrols and mock
battles have been proceeding smoothly.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.250
That's because I was facing you, Wing Commander,

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:58.210
Imperial Government of Karlsland Air Force

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:58.210
Flight Lieutenant Heidemarie W. Schnaufer

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.210
No matter how I approached I couldn't
quite catch you. It's inevitable.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.570
If we were using the same
Striker, I'd have been in trouble.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.930
Alright, the formalities have been completed.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.600
From today on, you'll be under my command.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.310
Understood.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.520
I'm sorry, taking in your squad
so soon after your arrival.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:24.180
It's no problem. Strengthening our
front lines is most important.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:29.540
Thanks to this I can forward my
accumulated paperwork to headquarters.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.300
Listen up, Hartmann.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.810
As a soldier of Karsland, you must always
maintain alertness on the battlefield,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:53.290
and be able to quickly respond to
any situation, but you...

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.230
Imperial Government of Karlsland Air Force

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.230
Flight Lieutenant Gertrud Barkhorn

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.900
But you always—!

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:59.830
Do you think Miyafuji is back in Fuso by now?

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.820
Imperial Government of Karlsland Air Force

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.820
Flight Officer Erica Hartmann

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:04.320
It <i>has</i> been a while, hasn't it.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.170
Wait, don't change the subject!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.650
A truck?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:11.860
I didn't hear about supplies coming.

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.740
That's...

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.080
Ursula! Yaho!

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.590
It's been a while, Nee-sama.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.590
Imperial Government of Karlsland Air Force

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.590
Flight Officer Ursula Hartmann

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.350
Ursula, what's the occasion?

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:27.320
I've brought some gifts for you all.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.470
Gifts?! Lemme see!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.600
Here. This is yours, Nee-sama.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.190
Yay! Sweets!

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.020
This is for Wing Commander Minna.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.600
It's coffee from Amazonas.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.620
And this is for Lieutenant Barkhorn.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:44.860
W-W-What is this...

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:48.920
It's a traditional dress from
southern Karsland called a "dirndl".

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.630
I believe it suits you.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.760
Ah, right, thanks.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.460
There's still more.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.420
Well then, please unload it.

00:05:58.420 --> 00:05:59.500
Roger.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.270
This is a curved barrel rifle.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.900
Simplified air-to-air homing missile.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.050
Flight capable flamethrower.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.260
Sonic cannon.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:14.880
As well as the MK-214 50mm cannon.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.340
Improved from the previous BK-5,

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:20.310
Its speed and penetration
power have been enhanced.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.040
Eh... This again?

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:26.640
It's true that this is very powerful,

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:29.410
But it's too heavy, even I can't fly with it.

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.170
It's alright.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.620
That's what the Jet is for.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:37.920
No, no, no!

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:40.370
You definitely can't use it!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:46.070
But the Jet's power is absolutely
needed to use the 50mm cannon.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.150
There's no other option.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.220
But something horrible happened last time!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.520
Did you forget?!

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.320
You'll go out of control and crash again!

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.510
You needn't worry.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:02.750
From the latest test results of the
HeS-011 magic engine,

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:06.410
I found that the energy
consumption was uncontrolled.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:13.540
This time, I've implemented a two-stage fuel injector
and a modified throttle on the Juma-004-D,

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:18.120
as well as increased the output
power of the magic engine,

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:25.540
and added a speed adjuster so it won't
over-consume magical power.

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:29.300
Basically, this time I won't crash, right?

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:30.520
Correct.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.330
Because output power has increased,

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:40.560
According to calculations, stable flight can be achieved at
more than 800 km/h even when using the 50mm cannon.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.060
That's absolutely spectacular.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.690
But it probably won't fly well!

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:49.440
Which is why we need the combat troops to test it.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.710
Understood. I'll do it.

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:53.770
No, no! You can't!

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:55.720
What now, Hartmann?

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:59.060
Besides I'm the one testing it, not you!

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.210
Hmph! Minna won't allow it!

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:02.720
I'll allow it.

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:03.960
Why?!

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:10.940
The Jet Strikers may play an important
role in recapturing Karsland.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:15.810
Besides, there will always be trouble in
the development of new weapons.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:19.080
Ursula-san is here to oversee everything, right?

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.980
Aren't you worried, Minna?

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:22.980
It will be okay.

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.530
We know what problems to
expect from previous test experience,

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:29.730
So Trude will be able to make corrections.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.900
Still...

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.410
Delicious!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.430
This coffee from Amazonas is really good!

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.410
You've been bought!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:47.520
Once again here are some safety pointers:

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:52.450
Before reaching flight capable speeds,
please do not adjust the throttle.

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:57.050
Also, to prevent the engine from stalling,
please do not rapidly accelerate or decelerate.

00:08:57.490 --> 00:08:58.810
Understood.

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.410
Launching!

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.590
The acceleration period is pretty long.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:14.690
Because it has been changed to
adapt to different energy outputs,

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:18.490
We need some time to see
the amount required for lift off.

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.160
Takes a long time to climb too.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.490
That's true.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:34.050
It's going in such a large
circle. Turning is bad too.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:39.000
Nee-sama, as I said before,
that's just how the Jet is.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.060
What do you mean by that?!

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:45.380
The Jet and the usual Strikers are different.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:49.560
The Jet promotes change from
each individual Witch's combat style,

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:55.210
As it reaches the enemy at high speeds and
utilizes large firepower to destroy enemies.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:03.100
You're right, once it's accelerated it's pretty fast.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.960
This is Barkhorn. I've reached
the previously recorded speed,

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.950
<i>and I don't feel any drain on my magical energy.</i>

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:11.550
<i>This could work!</i>

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:17.530
We've reached 800 km/h.
Please start the weapons test.

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:18.360
<i>Roger.</i>

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:27.410
It's really powerful.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:29.520
Medium-types would be completely blown apart.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.040
But they all missed.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:37.160
Because of its large firepower,
it's difficult to handle the recoil.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.030
We still can't use it in real combat.

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:46.150
Look at that, like I said. The Jet is no good.

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.820
No. The previous abnormalities
have already been corrected.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:52.840
There may be drawbacks, but it more than makes
up for them by being extremely powerful.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.210
Although, its accuracy would
be terrible in real combat.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:01.720
It seems to be because the Jet hasn't been
calibrated to absorb recoil from the 50mm cannon.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:05.820
Once it's been adjusted, it would
be indespensable in combat.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:06.970
Any ideas to fix it?

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.850
There needs to be adjustments
to the magic stabilizers.

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.480
And magic shock absorbers,

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.150
I'm heading back.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.990
Ah. Nee-sama, wait.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.260
What the heck is this?!

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.770
This is the BF-109, Zwei Link.

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:28.970
It can connect units of the same model

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:33.420
To increase output power, climb speed, flight distance, and weight capacity.

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:37.800
This is my unit! Why did you
add that without asking?!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.730
I already had Commander Minna's approval.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:46.860
Because of this unit's ability, it's best
for twins like you two to test it.

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:52.530
She's already here. You should help your
sister out once in a while, Hartmann.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:54.710
Tch, I get it.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:01.450
If we aren't on the same
wavelength, it will be hard to control.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.450
Before we start please confirm—

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:05.270
Got it.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:05.800
Let's go!

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:11.880
What's with Hartmann? She's so grumpy.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.390
Very impressive, Nee-sama.

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:20.310
It's your first time using the
Zwei Link yet your flight is so stable.

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:21.670
It's nothing.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:24.290
Nee-sama, is something troubling you?

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.930
It's nothing.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:37.280
N-Nee-sama, I can't follow if you suddenly accelerate.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:39.840
If you can't do this in real combat it's useless!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.630
But Nee-sama, the unit will...!

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:52.790
Oh no!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.430
This is bad. They're gonna crash!

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:04.940
Are you both okay?!

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:08.260
I-I'm fine.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:09.300
Heavy...

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:11.810
See, it's no good!

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.680
There are no problems with the unit.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.940
You didn't follow my instructions,
Nee-sama. That's why we crashed.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:22.000
That Jet and this thing
can't be used in real combat!

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.940
You keep bringing in dangerous things!

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.350
Even testing has procedures.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:29.450
Your actions are the
reason behind this accident.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:35.720
That's right, Erica. The reason for testing is to weed out
problems, not to see whether or not it can be used.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.710
In order to create new equipment
there needs to be tests.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:42.150
You ought to help out—

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.840
The 109 unit is more than enough for battle!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:47.440
Everything Ursula brings is useless!

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:56.440
Ursula...

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:05.580
Even though we failed this time,
valuable data was acquired.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.560
I will repair the unit as soon as possible.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:27.340
Huh?

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:30.020
She's not here.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.850
The unit's still broken too.

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:36.930
What's this?

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:45.000
"Went to the 3rd storage to
get tools for maintenance, Ursula."

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:47.920
Huh? She's not still mad?

00:14:56.030 --> 00:14:57.450
It's pretty good.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.140
Isn't it?

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.980
Ursula-san should be back around noon,

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.170
should we make lunch for her?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.270
Sounds good.

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.050
Morning.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.970
Ah, good morning.

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:12.170
You're late, Hartmann. Where were you?

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:15.460
I'm sorry. We've already finished eating.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:16.960
That's fine.

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:19.870
Well, what do you think, Hartmann?

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:24.750
You look weird!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:32.190
T-That's not it, Trude! It looks good on you!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:39.000
Medium-type spotted. Incoming from the west.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.750
<i>According to reports, it's a scout.</i>

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.310
We need to sortie, Trude.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.440
Roger.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:49.010
Erica.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:50.510
You're on standby.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:52.510
Eh? Why?!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.010
Your Striker still needs repairs.

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:13.070
The enemy is a regular scout, right?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.660
According to previous encounter
patterns, that's correct.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:19.160
<i>Okay. Let's finish this and get back by noon!</i>

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.310
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:38.070
Minna. We should be able to see it by now but...

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.640
It seems like the enemy isn't a scout.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:41.620
What?

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.690
I've been able to feel the enemy
coming. It's in there.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.400
In there?

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.310
You don't mean—?!

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:49.270
In the cumulonimbus cloud?!

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:52.320
Yes. The enemy seems like a combat type.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:55.570
And it's using the cumulonimbus cloud...

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:59.700
The inside is full of rising
air, strong wind, and hail.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.200
<i>And visibility is pretty much zero.</i>

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.550
<i>Combat in there would be impossible.</i>

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:09.230
There it is!

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:23.870
It's armor is too thick. We have to get closer.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:26.940
I'll move in! Cover me!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.940
<i>You can't! You won't be able to evade in that wind!</i>

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.290
<i>We're in a trap!</i>

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:33.960
<i>Well, what now?!</i>

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:40.890
That's it. We'll use that!

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.320
It's in the clouds again....

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:48.460
Minna!

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:53.960
The 50mm cannon. With it we can shoot
the enemy down at a distance!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.800
But you'll need the Jet to use the 50mm!

00:17:57.800 --> 00:17:59.300
The adjustments aren't ready yet!

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:03.520
That Neuroi  is troublesome. If we
hesitate any longer it'll advance!

00:18:05.490 --> 00:18:08.940
I understand. I'll slow it down then. Go get it!

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:10.310
Roger!

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:20.550
It divided?!

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:24.450
It wants to follow Trude? I won't let it!

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:34.210
It split again?!

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.310
<i>The enemy split apart?!</i>

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:38.390
<i>Yes. It's heading in your direction.</i>

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:39.720
<i>I can see 12.</i>

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:42.110
<i>Minna, you head back first!</i>

00:18:42.110 --> 00:18:45.110
<i>That won't do. I can't let it go now!</i>

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.050
Finally got one.

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:00.890
That was difficult.

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:03.270
Have I gotten dull because of a desk job?

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:19.320
The winds are too strong!

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:39.220
St. Trond Base. This is Barkhorn!

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:42.200
Please ready the Jet Striker and the 50mm cannon!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:45.700
<i>Load the 50mm with steel shells. Quick!</i>

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.700
Roger. Jet Striker, ready for launch.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:51.880
Eh? What did you say about the hangar?

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:52.430
What?!

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:56.850
Erica Hartmann.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:57.690
Launching!

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:08.440
St. Trond Base, I'm preparing to land.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:10.780
Please ready the support cannons!

00:20:10.780 --> 00:20:14.940
<i>Lieutenant, just now Flying Officer Hartmann...</i>

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.480
Hey! What's that? I can't hear you!

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:18.280
Hey!

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.440
Trude!

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:24.220
Hartmann, you—!

00:20:24.760 --> 00:20:27.090
I'm going to borrow this for a bit, okay?

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:36.420
She can use the Jet so well so quickly...

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:38.440
Hey! Where are you going, Hartmann?!

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.940
The Jet isn't listening to me!

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:44.400
Bastard!

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:49.230
Aw man, don't move!

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:51.460
Don't bother with those small fries, Hartmann!

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:52.140
But—!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:56.020
You're here to help Minna right? I'll cover you!

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.310
Go, quickly!

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.040
Roger!

00:21:08.050 --> 00:21:10.140
Right where I want you!

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:18.350
Your opponent is me!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.980
I'm gonna crash!

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:28.070
I'm surrounded!

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.060
You can't suddenly adjust the throttle.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:43.310
You'll cause an incomplete combustion and begin to stall, Nee-sama.

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:44.320
Ursula!

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:45.920
Ursula!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:56.800
I'm saved.

00:21:56.800 --> 00:21:59.080
Ursula! Didn't you leave?

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:02.810
I did. But something didn't feel right...

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:05.050
Anyways, I brought this with me.

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:07.500
Is that a Jet too?

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:12.310
Yes. This is the HE-162, a simplified prototype Jet.

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:15.560
Ah! That's right!

00:22:15.560 --> 00:22:19.670
Ursula! Minna's in trouble! We need to hurry!

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:23.210
Nee-sama, will you listen to my instructions?

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:25.210
Sure, sure, I'll listen!

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:28.360
Well then, please take a deep breath.

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:31.150
Widen your mouth and breathe in.

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:32.800
G-Got it.

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.070
Breathe out.

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:38.880
Breathe in.

00:22:40.150 --> 00:22:41.000
Stop!

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:51.690
It's working! Good job Ursula!

00:22:51.690 --> 00:22:54.980
Nee-sama, please focus on the 50mm cannon.

00:22:54.980 --> 00:22:57.260
Allow me to control the unit.

00:22:57.260 --> 00:22:58.140
Roger!

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:01.770
What amazing synergy...

00:23:02.360 --> 00:23:05.040
They're the only two who could pull it off.

00:23:06.450 --> 00:23:07.300
Minna!

00:23:17.150 --> 00:23:18.520
There's four left...

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:21.020
But I'm almost out of ammo.

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:24.450
I wonder if I can hang on until Trude returns?

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:34.330
Right, there' the big one too.

00:23:44.820 --> 00:23:45.540
I'm out?!

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:52.020
Minna!

00:23:55.030 --> 00:23:57.110
Sorry for the wait!

00:23:57.110 --> 00:24:00.680
Erica! Flying Officer Ursula! How?

00:24:04.640 --> 00:24:06.970
It sure does love hide and seek.

00:24:06.970 --> 00:24:08.950
But that's useless now.

00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:12.280
This is Minna. I have a lot of
questions, but I'll leave it for later.

00:24:12.830 --> 00:24:16.390
<i>The enemy's main body is in the
cumulonimbus cloud. I'm unable to lure it out.</i>

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:18.770
<i>Attack it at range from outside the cloud.</i>

00:24:18.770 --> 00:24:20.850
<i>Let me give you directions.</i>

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:23.270
So this is Commander Minna's inherent magic.

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:25.270
Yeah! It's called Space Understanding!

00:24:25.890 --> 00:24:29.780
<i>Maintain this speed. To the
right by 3 degrees, upwards by 5.</i>

00:24:30.710 --> 00:24:33.550
3, 2, 1, now!

00:24:40.010 --> 00:24:41.030
Got it!

00:24:41.030 --> 00:24:42.310
It's too shallow.

00:24:42.310 --> 00:24:47.300
Adjust for recoil by 0.3. Focus
magical energy on the barrel.

00:24:50.190 --> 00:24:52.600
The next shot will be the last, Nee-sama.

00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:53.580
Got it!

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:17.200
Wow! It looks great on you!

00:25:18.990 --> 00:25:23.460
Thank you. But, it's a little tight.

00:25:25.400 --> 00:25:26.460
I see.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:29.960
Such troublesome things happened while I was gone.

00:25:30.480 --> 00:25:34.470
How is it, Hartmann? Don't you want to use the Jet now?

00:25:35.900 --> 00:25:36.930
Nope.

00:25:36.930 --> 00:25:39.220
Why? Aren't there combat results now?

00:25:40.420 --> 00:25:42.970
Well, if there were two people using it, then maybe.

00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:17.330
Deep down in our hearts we think to ourselves

00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:17.330
itsu datte kono mune no oku himeteru

00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:23.500
"I won't lose to anyone, I'm strong"

00:26:17.810 --> 00:26:23.500
darenimo makenai tsuyoi omoi

00:26:23.770 --> 00:26:29.440
Sometimes when we take a step forward

00:26:23.770 --> 00:26:29.440
dare datte ippo fumidasu tokiniwa

00:26:29.800 --> 00:26:35.220
We lose our way, get afraid, but continue on

00:26:29.800 --> 00:26:35.220
arekore mayou kedo osorezu ni susume

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:47.520
My dreams overflow with magic, I want to change the sorrow of this world

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:47.520
yume ga afureru mahou de kono sekai no kanashimi o kaete ku

00:26:47.810 --> 00:26:55.000
Even a smile will become a strength

00:26:47.810 --> 00:26:55.000
itsu datte egao ga tsuyosa ni naru

00:26:56.400 --> 00:27:02.180
Let's fly away, far from here, and aim at the heavens

00:26:56.400 --> 00:27:02.180
FLY AWAY koko kara oozora megakete

00:27:02.500 --> 00:27:08.300
Spread your wings of hope and get ready to soar

00:27:02.500 --> 00:27:08.300
kibou no tsubasa o hirogete tobitate

00:27:08.410 --> 00:27:14.210
If you can change the world, then go ahead

00:27:08.410 --> 00:27:14.210
CHANGE THE WORLD kimi nara kaete yukeru kara

00:27:14.420 --> 00:27:20.930
All you need is one chance to be courageous

00:27:14.420 --> 00:27:20.930
meguri aeta kiseki ga yuuki ni kawaru yo

00:27:28.780 --> 00:27:32.230
Yoshika-chan!

00:27:32.230 --> 00:27:34.630
I'm coming in!

00:27:35.060 --> 00:27:37.890
You've been back in Fuso for a week now.

00:27:37.890 --> 00:27:40.150
So, how have your studies been?

00:27:40.150 --> 00:27:42.550
It's alright I guess...

00:27:42.550 --> 00:27:45.350
Medical books are kinda hard.

00:27:45.350 --> 00:27:47.950
Ah, this photograph...

00:27:47.950 --> 00:27:50.860
It arrived from Europe yesterday.

00:27:50.860 --> 00:27:53.660
It looks like Hartmann-san's sister is there!

00:27:53.660 --> 00:27:58.290
Huh? By Hartmann-san you mean
one of the world's greatest aces?

00:27:58.290 --> 00:28:01.360
Ah, I think they mentioned that...

00:28:01.360 --> 00:28:05.410
Really! Even though you were
in the same unit. What a waste!

00:28:05.410 --> 00:28:07.910
A w-waste?

00:28:07.910 --> 00:28:10.460
But it seems they're all really happy!

00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:14.800
Barkhorn-san is adorable!

00:28:15.670 --> 00:28:18.670
To Be Continued

00:28:19.860 --> 00:28:24.880
Next time: Strike Witches
Operation Victory Arrow volume 2!

00:28:24.880 --> 00:28:26.640
Goddess of the Aegean Sea.

00:28:26.640 --> 00:28:29.620
Featuring Shirley-san and Lucchini-san!

00:28:29.620 --> 00:28:31.010
Please look forward to it!
